&lt;h2&gt;Hyperefficient&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I am going to try some small experiments based on reading this book.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.cathalanddad.com/images/hyperefficient/20250404_122330.jpg" alt="Cover" width="400"/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The first one will be based on the idea of structuring a work session. I am going to try this and see if it works better than the Pomodoro method. I often find Pomodoro hard to stick with if I am working on something boring and interrupting if I am doing something better. The 90 minute length of these sessions should help.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.cathalanddad.com/images/hyperefficient/20250404_122529.jpg" alt="Cover" width="400"/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Experiment detail&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Try 2 of these 90 minute sessions this afternoon. Note how they go and decide whether or not to continue with this.&lt;/p&gt;</content><category term="Books"></category></entry></feed>